WEBVTT

00:00.525 --> 00:03.834
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.835 --> 00:07.025
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.026 --> 00:10.762
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.763 --> 00:13.765
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.766 --> 00:17.135
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.136 --> 00:20.372
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.373 --> 00:21.973
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:21.974 --> 00:23.508
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.509 --> 00:28.942
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.836 --> 00:35.276
Hey, do you think homeless people

00:35.277 --> 00:37.002
ever have sex with each other?

00:37.003 --> 00:38.905
Probably. But I don't
want to think about it.

00:38.906 --> 00:40.673
I know for a fact they do.

00:40.674 --> 00:42.508
I spend most of my day breaking up

00:42.509 --> 00:45.394
- in-progress homeless sex.
- I bet it stink.

00:45.395 --> 00:46.996
Oh, it stink all right.

00:46.997 --> 00:49.565
So we talking group stuff
or just one-on-one?

00:49.566 --> 00:52.789
Oh, anything goes. Whatever
you can fit under a tarp.

00:52.790 --> 00:55.293
There's a major hot spot
behind the Dumpster

00:55.294 --> 00:56.541
at The Cheesecake Factory.

00:56.542 --> 00:58.740
Hey, what's up with the menus
at The Cheesecake Factory?

00:58.741 --> 01:00.276
Why they got to be so big?

01:00.277 --> 01:02.278
Yeah, and why does their menu have ads?

01:02.279 --> 01:04.780
I go there for dinner, not
to shop for appliances.

01:04.781 --> 01:07.149
Hey, you know what,
guys? This right here,

01:07.150 --> 01:09.318
this rambling, boring
conversation containing

01:09.319 --> 01:11.637
already-made-before observations,

01:11.638 --> 01:13.088
this could be a podcast.

01:13.089 --> 01:14.923
Ah. That's actually not a bad idea.

01:14.924 --> 01:16.692
Really? A podcast? Don't you have to be

01:16.693 --> 01:18.527
some sort of whiz kid to do those?

01:18.528 --> 01:21.263
Uh, definitely not... anyone
with a computer can make one.

01:21.264 --> 01:23.132
Well, that's it... We're "anyone."

01:23.133 --> 01:25.601
Let's do a podcast from
right here in the booth.

01:25.602 --> 01:26.335
Who's in?

01:26.336 --> 01:27.435
- Let's do it!
- Yeah, sure.

01:27.436 --> 01:29.438
Is it happening? Are we doing it now?

01:29.439 --> 01:31.473
Awesome! We haven't done
anything as a group

01:31.474 --> 01:33.054
since we went birdwatching.

01:33.476 --> 01:34.877
Guys, look.

01:34.878 --> 01:36.979
It's the yellow-headed puffin face.

01:36.980 --> 01:38.314
Oh! Ooh!

01:38.315 --> 01:40.115
It's a solitary creature.

01:40.116 --> 01:43.152
It's feathered crown is
designed to scare away mates.

01:43.153 --> 01:44.620
It's known to swell its face

01:44.621 --> 01:46.055
to assert dominance when threatened.

01:46.056 --> 01:47.856
What does it eat, Peter?

01:47.857 --> 01:50.627
Gin and whatever's in
the bowl at the airport bar.

01:57.146 --> 01:59.696
I said, damn, what a
wild couple of days.

01:59.697 --> 02:01.628
Anyways, 'sup with you guys?

02:01.629 --> 02:04.482
Sorry, amigo, not interested.

02:07.135 --> 02:09.637
This is what happens when
you lick your spilled latte

02:09.638 --> 02:10.770
off the steering wheel.

02:10.771 --> 02:12.340
She did that. She's gross.

02:12.341 --> 02:14.141
- Lois, are you okay?
- Ugh. Yeah.

02:14.142 --> 02:16.544
It's just my allergies.
They've been awful.

02:16.545 --> 02:18.746
I can't figure out what it is.

02:19.714 --> 02:21.218
Maybe it's Brian.

02:21.219 --> 02:23.021
He practically sleeps on top of you.

02:23.022 --> 02:24.556
<i>You could be allergic to him.</i>

02:24.557 --> 02:25.990
Hey, here's an idea, Chris...

02:25.991 --> 02:27.559
why don't you mind your own business?

02:27.560 --> 02:29.260
You know, I did read that people

02:29.261 --> 02:31.196
could develop allergies to their pets.

02:31.197 --> 02:33.832
Brian, maybe you shouldn't
sleep in our bedroom

02:33.833 --> 02:35.990
- for a little while.
- What?

02:35.991 --> 02:37.435
Well, then where am I supposed to sleep?

02:37.436 --> 02:40.399
How about in your own
apartment, like a grown-up?

02:40.400 --> 02:41.840
Do you have a problem with me, Chris?

02:41.841 --> 02:43.875
Why don't you sleep in Stewie's room?

02:43.876 --> 02:45.443
There's plenty of space.

02:45.444 --> 02:48.546
Roomies? Dude! This'll be so ill!

02:48.547 --> 02:50.448
<i>- Who are you?
- I'll tell you who.</i>

02:50.449 --> 02:51.750
Your new roommate!

02:53.085 --> 02:54.719
I'm gonna go take a shower

02:54.720 --> 02:57.222
so I can blow my nose into my hands.

02:58.357 --> 03:00.558
Damn it! I hate this house.

03:00.559 --> 03:03.051
- Morning, honey!
- Go to hell!

03:07.050 --> 03:09.468
All right, you guys, podcast time.

03:09.469 --> 03:12.163
We got the equipment and the
perfect business plan...

03:12.164 --> 03:15.373
give our show away for free, and
tell no one how to find it.

03:15.374 --> 03:16.708
Ready?

03:16.709 --> 03:18.610
Hey there, the Net,

03:18.611 --> 03:22.007
<i>welcome to the first episode
of Thanks for the Clamories.</i>

03:22.008 --> 03:23.715
I'm here with Glenn Quagmire,

03:23.716 --> 03:26.084
- Hi.
- Cleveland Brown...

03:26.085 --> 03:27.719
- and...
- Hello.

03:27.720 --> 03:29.387
And Joe Swanson.

03:29.388 --> 03:30.491
Yo-zah!

03:30.492 --> 03:32.157
All right, Quagmire,
what do you got for us?

03:32.158 --> 03:33.725
Let's make a clam-ory.

03:33.726 --> 03:36.161
Okay, this is yes or no.
Y-You ready, Peter?

03:36.162 --> 03:38.163
Yes or no. French toast.

03:38.164 --> 03:39.964
- Yes.
- French fries.

03:39.965 --> 03:41.733
- Yes.
- French kissing.

03:41.734 --> 03:44.529
I-I don't know. These
questions are weird.

03:44.530 --> 03:45.603
Okay, okay, someone else.

03:45.604 --> 03:47.472
Cleveland, yes or no.

03:47.473 --> 03:50.308
- Velcro shoes.
- Hmm, Velcro shoes.

03:50.309 --> 03:52.310
Woo-whee, this is a tough one.

03:52.311 --> 03:55.079
I remember the first time I
saw me a pair of 'cro's.

03:55.080 --> 03:57.148
They were on the feet of Spunky Tesik.

03:57.149 --> 03:58.683
Man, they was dandy...

03:58.684 --> 04:00.685
Every time we played touch football,

04:00.686 --> 04:03.154
Spunky would step in a pile of dog poo.

04:03.155 --> 04:06.357
You can wash a shoe, but you
can't really wash a lace.

04:06.358 --> 04:08.293
That's why Spunky made the change.

04:08.294 --> 04:10.328
That's the thing about Velcro shoes.

04:10.329 --> 04:12.797
Quiet going on, noisy coming off.

04:12.798 --> 04:15.633
That rip! Spunky's mama
thought he was an intruder.

04:15.634 --> 04:17.746
Shot him right in the face.

04:17.747 --> 04:19.731
Had an open casket at the funeral.

04:19.732 --> 04:21.306
But only open on the middle part...

04:21.307 --> 04:24.509
To this day, every time I
see a pile of dog doo,

04:24.510 --> 04:26.978
I take a step in it just for Spunky.

04:26.979 --> 04:29.681
So to answer the question,
I'm gonna have to say

04:29.682 --> 04:31.783
<i>both yes and no.</i>

04:31.784 --> 04:33.985
All right, that's all the time we got.

04:33.986 --> 04:37.018
I'd like to thank our sponsor,
the U.S. Postal Service.

04:37.019 --> 04:39.324
When you want something
expensive thrown on your porch

04:39.325 --> 04:42.295
and stolen, you want the
U.S. Postal Service.

04:42.296 --> 04:43.777
What the hell was that?

04:43.778 --> 04:46.340
I know! Cleveland, you
ruined the whole podcast.

04:46.341 --> 04:48.666
Yeah, if I wanted to hear a black
guy ramble like a lunatic,

04:48.667 --> 04:50.902
<i>- I'd watch Family Feud.
- Yeah, I mean, that was worse</i>

04:50.903 --> 04:54.372
than an Italian guy describing
someone's sexuality.

04:54.373 --> 04:56.040
Anyway, my brother Louie, he's a...

04:56.041 --> 04:58.243
he's a little off to the side, you know?

04:58.244 --> 05:00.245
Uh, foofy. Uh, up to the knuckle.

05:00.246 --> 05:02.247
He's a... he's a backwards mechanic.

05:02.248 --> 05:04.315
- Likes to play in the dirt.
- You mean gay?

05:04.316 --> 05:05.984
Mama!

05:05.985 --> 05:07.252
<i>Marone! Peter!</i>

05:07.253 --> 05:09.153
Mama, Louie's not gay, he's...

05:09.154 --> 05:11.489
he's creative.

05:17.392 --> 05:19.597
Hey, Stewie, thanks for
letting me stay in your room.

05:19.598 --> 05:22.033
<i>Oh, Brian, please... It's our room now.</i>

05:22.034 --> 05:23.434
Hey, what are we gonna do tonight?

05:23.435 --> 05:25.336
Ooh, maybe we should watch
that movie about Freud

05:25.337 --> 05:27.338
where Michael Fassbender
repeatedly spanks

05:27.339 --> 05:29.374
Keira Knightley to orgasm?

05:29.375 --> 05:31.543
- You saw that movie?
- I saw that scene.

05:33.078 --> 05:35.413
<i>So, I was thinking this
could be your area.</i>

05:35.414 --> 05:37.115
Okay, yeah, yeah. This is great.

05:37.116 --> 05:39.350
And fair warning... Some
of the books are pop-up,

05:39.351 --> 05:41.419
- so don't be alarmed.
- Aah! Son of a bitch!

05:41.420 --> 05:43.421
Frickin' bird came out of nowhere!

05:43.422 --> 05:45.757
You know, I have a good
feeling about this, Brian.

05:45.758 --> 05:47.625
After all, you certainly
can't be any worse

05:47.626 --> 05:49.110
than the last roommate I had.

05:51.615 --> 05:53.264
- What the...?
- Please don't cry.

05:53.265 --> 05:55.099
She's already very angry at me.

05:55.100 --> 05:57.468
<i>Peter, where are you?
You will wash your hands</i>

05:57.469 --> 05:58.736
after you poop.

05:58.737 --> 05:59.971
Shh, shh.

05:59.972 --> 06:00.970
I won't.

06:05.128 --> 06:06.611
<i>You know, this is exciting.</i>

06:06.612 --> 06:08.217
Our second podcast.

06:08.218 --> 06:09.414
All right, but listen up, Cleveland.

06:09.415 --> 06:11.416
No more of your long stories, all right?

06:11.417 --> 06:13.418
Yeah, people aren't used
to boring podcasts.

06:13.419 --> 06:16.754
Oh, I'm sorry. I suppose they
ought to call me "Jelly,"

06:16.755 --> 06:19.057
'cause sometimes I get on a roll.

06:19.058 --> 06:20.291
That. That.

06:20.292 --> 06:22.493
J... N-None of that.

06:22.494 --> 06:24.929
<i>Welcome once again to
Thanks for the Clamories.</i>

06:24.930 --> 06:27.165
Okay, common question that
everybody thinks about.

06:27.166 --> 06:30.141
How many fourth-graders you
think you could take at once?

06:30.142 --> 06:31.803
- What?
- I mean, obviously, if you had to fight

06:31.804 --> 06:33.805
against a million
fourth-graders, you'd lose.

06:33.806 --> 06:35.807
So, like, what's...
what's the real number?

06:35.808 --> 06:38.059
Like, what's the legitimate
number of fourth-graders

06:38.060 --> 06:39.811
that you could successfully take on?

06:39.812 --> 06:41.567
Let's say a hundred.
That sounds reasonable.

06:41.568 --> 06:43.243
Oh, no way. A hundred and you're dead.

06:43.244 --> 06:45.220
- Why are we fighting, now?
- 'Cause they're idiots.

06:45.221 --> 06:46.851
Did they say something about my mother?

06:46.852 --> 06:49.120
What...? Yes. Okay, yeah,
yeah, we'll say yes.

06:49.121 --> 06:52.315
- Oh, then a baker's dozen.
- What kind of weapons?

06:52.316 --> 06:53.874
Only what's available in the schoolyard.

06:53.875 --> 06:56.594
You could really mess up some
kids with a chain from a swing.

06:56.595 --> 06:59.014
Just da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da!

06:59.015 --> 07:01.499
All right, tell you what I'd do,
I'd back into a bathroom stall,

07:01.500 --> 07:03.801
and just start kickin'.
Dead! Dead! Dead!

07:03.802 --> 07:06.170
Keep comin'! Dead! Give
'em a narrow entry point,

07:06.171 --> 07:07.639
make 'em come in single file.

07:07.640 --> 07:09.941
Dead! Dead! Anyway, I
guess I'm trying to say

07:09.942 --> 07:11.342
800 fourth-graders.

07:11.343 --> 07:13.111
Why are we talking about killing kids?

07:13.112 --> 07:15.446
People are gonna hate this.
Peter, do something else, quick.

07:15.447 --> 07:18.616
I'll-I'll... uh, what if I
play some kick-ass music?

07:21.120 --> 07:22.654
Kick-ass? This is not kick-ass.

07:22.655 --> 07:24.722
Wait, hang on, hang on,
I'll find something.

07:26.859 --> 07:28.493
You're playing two songs at once.

07:28.494 --> 07:30.161
- What even is this?
- I-I don't know.

07:30.162 --> 07:31.529
I'm just pressing buttons!

07:31.530 --> 07:33.731
I got to admit, it does have a groove.

07:33.732 --> 07:36.067
Look! Those people are
even dancing to it.

07:39.872 --> 07:42.840
Aw, great! I accidentally
started Chris's birth video.

07:42.841 --> 07:45.510
Ow! O-O-O-O-O-Ow! Ow!

07:45.511 --> 07:46.678
Ow!

07:46.679 --> 07:48.713
Ow! Kill me!

07:48.714 --> 07:50.915
Hey, what's that song you're playing?

07:50.916 --> 07:53.885
I don't know, it's just random
garbage from my computer.

07:53.886 --> 07:56.154
Oh, you're a deejay! That's perfect!

07:56.155 --> 07:58.756
I own a nightclub for cocaine
people and Armenians.

07:58.757 --> 08:00.925
I need noise. You available?

08:00.926 --> 08:02.326
- We're in!
- Great!

08:02.327 --> 08:04.667
I'll see you guys Wednesday at 2:00 a.m.

08:05.364 --> 08:07.665
What the hell was that? We're
supposed to be doing a podcast.

08:07.666 --> 08:09.067
Peter, I don't know if you noticed,

08:09.068 --> 08:10.935
but the podcast was a disaster.

08:10.936 --> 08:13.705
<i>Yeah, and we were looking for
something to do as a foursome.</i>

08:13.706 --> 08:15.707
But how can I be a deejay?

08:15.708 --> 08:18.376
I'm just a guy with a laptop
and an inflated self-image.

08:18.377 --> 08:19.777
Trust me, you're perfect.

08:19.778 --> 08:22.046
All right, sounds good. Let's do this.

08:22.047 --> 08:25.416
<i>Okay, but hold on. I got
four quarters on Golden Tee.</i>

08:26.919 --> 08:28.219
How am I doing?

08:28.220 --> 08:30.121
Good job, Joe! A hole in one!

08:30.122 --> 08:32.107
He just
keeps switching clubs.

08:37.690 --> 08:40.366
Kids, time for dinner.
Where's your father?

08:40.367 --> 08:42.392
I think he's getting ready
for his deejay gig.

08:42.393 --> 08:43.278
His what?

08:44.749 --> 08:47.397
Hmm. Still a trace of melody.

08:47.398 --> 08:49.399
I'll just add some power tools.

08:53.238 --> 08:56.473
Yeah. Yeah, I'd drink vodka
and Gatorade to that.

08:56.474 --> 08:58.642
Peter, since when are you a deejay?

08:58.643 --> 08:59.895
Since some guy came in the Clam

08:59.896 --> 09:01.695
and heard my awesome jams and beats.

09:01.696 --> 09:03.531
Well, he's got the lingo down.

09:03.532 --> 09:04.632
Thanks, Chris.

09:04.633 --> 09:07.735
Now, scream...!

09:07.736 --> 09:10.071
<i>Hey, you are good at this, Dad.</i>

09:10.072 --> 09:12.948
Peter, knock it off.
You're a middle-aged man.

09:12.949 --> 09:14.542
You can't be a deejay.

09:14.543 --> 09:16.422
Why not? I could totally be a deejay.

09:16.423 --> 09:18.846
For God's sake, John Travolta's a pilot.

09:18.847 --> 09:20.748
This
is your captain speaking.

09:20.749 --> 09:22.650
We have reached our cruising altitude.

09:22.651 --> 09:26.253
It is now safe to take off
your wigs and be gay.

09:32.419 --> 09:33.741
Well, what's all this?

09:33.742 --> 09:35.973
Oh, just some stuff I got
out of my storage unit.

09:35.974 --> 09:37.775
Check this out. You'll love this.

09:37.776 --> 09:39.844
Do I look like a Terminator dog?

09:39.845 --> 09:41.646
- No.
- Yeah, I do.

09:41.647 --> 09:44.966
Look... I even brought Tom
Sizemore's Game of Life.

09:46.770 --> 09:49.987
<i>"Sell rights to Saving
Private Ryan residuals</i>

09:49.988 --> 09:52.097
to buy a case of Coors Light."

09:54.063 --> 09:57.497
"Steal your son's wallet
while he's in the shower."

09:59.436 --> 10:01.469
"Miss audition."

10:03.353 --> 10:05.870
"Scoop someone's urine
from Starbucks toilet

10:05.871 --> 10:07.472
to pass drug test."

10:07.473 --> 10:10.174
Feels like we should be moving
these pieces backwards.

10:12.578 --> 10:15.012
Okay, let's make some noise

10:15.013 --> 10:18.049
for Deejay Peter and the Sound Slap!

10:20.586 --> 10:22.086
Giggity,
giggity, giggity, giggity,

10:22.087 --> 10:24.088
giggity, giggity, giggity,
giggity, giggity!

10:24.089 --> 10:26.357
Give it to 'em.

10:26.358 --> 10:28.025
Shut up, Meg.

10:28.026 --> 10:29.527
Sh-Sh-Shut up, Meg.

10:29.528 --> 10:31.162
Heh-heh-heh-heh-heh-heh.

10:31.163 --> 10:32.730
Butt scratcher! Butt scratcher!

10:34.433 --> 10:35.933
Peter, Peter, Peter...

10:35.934 --> 10:37.568
Roadhouse. Roadhouse.

10:37.569 --> 10:39.070
That's nasty. That's nasty.

10:39.071 --> 10:41.572
What? Wha-Wha-Wha-What?

10:41.573 --> 10:43.174
This place is awesome!

10:43.175 --> 10:45.510
Totally! And did you see Tom Sizemore

10:45.511 --> 10:47.745
in the bathroom with a ladle?

10:54.237 --> 10:55.987
You've been playing the exact same song

10:55.988 --> 10:57.488
for 14 hours.

10:57.489 --> 10:58.856
That means you're great.

10:58.857 --> 11:00.391
I was right about you, guy.

11:00.392 --> 11:03.261
Weird you turned that into a
compliment about yourself.

11:03.262 --> 11:04.759
Well, I'm on cocaine.

11:06.098 --> 11:08.766
My kid's baseball team
came in second place.

11:08.767 --> 11:10.535
I don't care about that.

11:10.536 --> 11:13.404
But listen, there's a big
music festival coming up.

11:13.405 --> 11:15.506
You've got some mad deejay skills.

11:15.507 --> 11:17.592
You could be our headliner.

11:19.596 --> 11:21.379
Electric Clam Festival?

11:21.380 --> 11:22.780
Yeah, it's gonna be awesome.

11:22.781 --> 11:24.749
- So what do you say?
- Well, I don't know.

11:24.750 --> 11:26.951
I-I should probably check with
the guys and see what they...

11:26.952 --> 11:28.553
What? You don't need the guys.

11:28.554 --> 11:31.689
I didn't see their fingers
press three buttons.

11:31.690 --> 11:33.858
Huh. I guess I do have a gift.

11:33.859 --> 11:34.892
So are you in?

11:34.893 --> 11:36.127
Yeah, that'd be amazing.

11:36.128 --> 11:37.395
Can I kiss you?

11:37.396 --> 11:39.130
- Excuse me?
- I don't know.

11:39.131 --> 11:41.098
Someone gave me a pill,
and now all I want to do

11:41.099 --> 11:42.567
is feel your jacket.

11:42.568 --> 11:45.036
Oh, yeah.

11:45.037 --> 11:47.255
No, no, stay here. Stay here.

11:51.972 --> 11:54.038
That. That. That. See,
listen. Right there.

11:54.039 --> 11:55.333
You can't hear that on a CD.

11:55.334 --> 11:56.647
Only the vinyl, man.

11:56.648 --> 11:59.951
I'm glad we hung out after
you struck out with my mom.

11:59.952 --> 12:02.753
You know, I could've used some
help folding these fitted sheets.

12:02.754 --> 12:04.655
- Who's this turd?
- Oh, this is Georgie.

12:04.656 --> 12:07.124
Brian, I never said you
could have guests.

12:07.125 --> 12:08.593
Hey, don't touch that.

12:08.594 --> 12:10.565
Okay, red flags flying.

12:10.566 --> 12:12.163
Look, I need him out of here.

12:12.164 --> 12:14.966
You can't kick him out. He's my
friend, and I live here, too.

12:14.967 --> 12:17.068
Not anymore. I want you out of my room.

12:17.069 --> 12:19.337
Well, it's not your room
anymore, it's our room.

12:19.338 --> 12:21.472
Lois said so, and I'm not leaving.

12:21.473 --> 12:24.242
I can't believe I ever wanted
you here in the first place.

12:24.243 --> 12:26.777
You're messy, you're
loud, and thanks to you,

12:26.778 --> 12:28.412
we've got a recurring flea problem.

12:32.435 --> 12:34.652
Hey, Bri. You want to hang out?

12:34.653 --> 12:36.654
Go away, Flea. You're not welcome here.

12:36.655 --> 12:38.489
And put on a shirt. You're 50.

12:38.490 --> 12:39.974
Actually, 54.

12:48.885 --> 12:51.335
Peter, I was plowing this
college chick last night,

12:51.336 --> 12:53.821
and I saw this flyer on her mini fridge.

12:56.693 --> 12:58.376
I thought we were all in this together.

12:58.377 --> 12:59.944
Well, yeah. That's the thing.

12:59.945 --> 13:02.280
A guy on cocaine told me I'm the talent.

13:02.281 --> 13:03.614
So what, you're just dropping us?

13:03.615 --> 13:05.449
Yeah, how could you just ditch us?

13:05.450 --> 13:07.852
All right, you know what? You
guys were riding my coattails.

13:07.853 --> 13:09.387
I carried you as long as I could,

13:09.388 --> 13:11.522
but Rob Kardashian's
gonna be at this thing,

13:11.523 --> 13:12.990
so I got to be at my best.

13:12.991 --> 13:14.458
Now, get out of here. I got to practice.

13:16.028 --> 13:17.295
Damn it, Peter. That's too loud.

13:17.296 --> 13:18.462
Turn it down.

13:18.463 --> 13:20.848
That isn't loud. This is.

13:22.919 --> 13:26.070
It's not loud until you
can feel your head bones.

13:26.071 --> 13:29.206
If you can't hack it, take a hike.

13:29.207 --> 13:30.675
Why's he being such a jerk?

13:30.676 --> 13:32.143
I don't know.

13:32.144 --> 13:33.744
We've always had each other's backs,

13:33.745 --> 13:35.379
like when we used to rob banks

13:35.380 --> 13:37.415
in lesser-known presidents masks.

13:37.416 --> 13:40.067
All right. Remember to
tell everyone who did this.

13:40.068 --> 13:42.202
Um. Who are you guys supposed to be?

13:42.203 --> 13:43.870
Oh, come
on. I'm James K. Polk.

13:43.871 --> 13:45.305
He's Millard Fillmore.

13:45.306 --> 13:46.873
He's William Henry Harrison.

13:46.874 --> 13:48.975
First president to die in office.

13:48.976 --> 13:50.276
You should've been FDR.

13:50.277 --> 13:51.444
Why?

13:51.445 --> 13:53.246
'Cause of the... you know.

13:53.247 --> 13:54.914
The wheelchair doesn't define me!

13:54.915 --> 13:56.749
And I'm Grover Cleveland.

13:56.750 --> 13:58.750
It's funny, 'cause my name's Cleveland.

13:58.751 --> 14:00.987
Aw, damn it, Cleveland.
Now we got to kill them all.

14:00.988 --> 14:02.956
This guy gets it first.

14:09.396 --> 14:11.297
Ugh. Didn't you hear the alarm?

14:12.125 --> 14:13.466
Peter, wake up.

14:13.467 --> 14:15.185
We're gonna be late for church.

14:15.769 --> 14:17.637
Are you even listening to me?

14:17.638 --> 14:19.572
You've got to stop coming home so late

14:19.573 --> 14:21.407
if you can't get up in
the morning, and...

14:45.984 --> 14:48.246
Oh, God. I can't hear Garfield.

14:48.247 --> 14:49.612
I've gone deaf.

14:54.801 --> 14:57.302
All right, now how long has
your husband smelled like this?

14:57.303 --> 14:59.999
Oh, no. That's just from
riding here in a hot car,

15:00.000 --> 15:02.206
but Dr. Hartman, what about his hearing?

15:02.207 --> 15:03.032
Hearing?

15:03.033 --> 15:04.668
This is a hospital, I'm not a lawyer.

15:04.669 --> 15:07.238
Oh, for God's sake, is my husband deaf?

15:07.239 --> 15:09.974
Well, there's only one way
to find out definitively.

15:09.975 --> 15:12.123
Hey stupid deaf guy!

15:12.645 --> 15:14.879
Well, I've gotten the
results back. He's deaf.

15:14.880 --> 15:16.414
This is horrible.

15:16.415 --> 15:18.216
This must be because of all that loud,

15:18.217 --> 15:20.985
blaring music he's been
playing in those nightclubs.

15:20.986 --> 15:23.054
What's going on? Can he fix it in time

15:23.055 --> 15:24.989
for me to deejay at the music festival?

15:24.990 --> 15:26.418
- No.
- What?

15:26.419 --> 15:28.162
- No!
- What?

15:29.274 --> 15:30.428
Are you sure?

15:30.429 --> 15:31.896
- Yes.
- What?

15:31.897 --> 15:34.467
Have a good life.

15:39.389 --> 15:41.137
Hey, guys, I don't know if you've heard,

15:41.138 --> 15:42.240
but I've gone deaf.

15:42.241 --> 15:43.541
- You what?
- What?

15:43.542 --> 15:44.742
Oh, you're ear crippled?

15:44.743 --> 15:45.944
I can't hear you, Joe.

15:45.945 --> 15:47.345
Here's a bag of Alpha-Bits.

15:47.346 --> 15:49.197
Please spell out what you're saying.

15:51.301 --> 15:52.951
Oh, there's no "L" s.

15:52.952 --> 15:54.852
By the way, I ate all the
"L" s. They're delicious.

15:54.853 --> 15:56.621
- They're my favorite ones.
- What are you talking about?

15:56.622 --> 15:58.423
- They all taste the same.
- What?

15:58.424 --> 16:00.058
Why don't you just text it to him?

16:00.059 --> 16:01.526
You know, that's a good idea.

16:01.527 --> 16:03.595
What the hell do you want?

16:03.596 --> 16:06.364
You told us you were a big shot deejay

16:06.365 --> 16:08.967
and didn't want anything to do with us.

16:10.102 --> 16:11.536
I don't think he can hear it.

16:11.537 --> 16:13.698
Oh, son of a bitch. Look at your phone.

16:14.640 --> 16:16.407
Oh, what do I want?

16:16.408 --> 16:18.727
Um, the Electric Clam
Festival's coming up,

16:18.728 --> 16:20.078
and I need your help.

16:20.079 --> 16:22.947
Now that I'm deaf, I can't
do it without you guys.

16:22.948 --> 16:24.749
Forget it. You told us to go to hell.

16:24.750 --> 16:26.284
Well, now you can go to hell.

16:26.285 --> 16:27.585
Oh, great. Thanks.

16:27.586 --> 16:29.053
I knew I could count on you guys.

16:29.054 --> 16:30.913
- But we said no.
- What?

16:35.579 --> 16:37.562
One, two, thr... ah, crap.

16:37.563 --> 16:39.715
One, two... come on.

16:39.716 --> 16:41.189
All right. This time
for the world record.

16:44.087 --> 16:45.970
Eww. What the hell is that?

16:45.971 --> 16:47.739
It's a ferret. Look at it, Brian.

16:47.740 --> 16:49.340
It's like a long rat.

16:49.341 --> 16:51.643
Like a living tail. Look at its feet.

16:51.644 --> 16:54.112
Eww. They're gross.
Why'd you get a ferret?

16:54.113 --> 16:55.980
All the worst roommates have ferrets.

16:55.981 --> 16:57.682
You want to pet it? It bites.

16:57.683 --> 16:59.951
I can't sleep with that monster in here.

16:59.952 --> 17:02.086
That's the idea. I want you out.

17:02.087 --> 17:04.355
This room belongs to
me and the ferret now.

17:04.356 --> 17:05.957
Why you being such a dick about this?

17:05.958 --> 17:08.860
Because. You're a pain
in the ass to live with.

17:09.359 --> 17:10.628
What did you just do?

17:10.629 --> 17:12.533
I just pushed a little bitch baby.

17:17.169 --> 17:18.703
Oh, Brian, there you are.

17:18.704 --> 17:20.304
I wanted to tell you
that you can come back

17:20.305 --> 17:21.773
and sleep in our room.

17:21.774 --> 17:23.174
What? I can?

17:23.175 --> 17:24.776
Yeah. Turns out it was Peter

17:24.777 --> 17:26.444
who was causing my allergies.

17:26.445 --> 17:28.379
He stuffed all our pillows with hay

17:28.380 --> 17:31.315
because he thought it looked
comfortable in cartoons.

17:31.778 --> 17:34.952
Wow. Then, I guess I'm moving out.

17:34.953 --> 17:36.104
I guess you are.

17:36.855 --> 17:38.489
Look, Stewie, I-I...

17:38.490 --> 17:40.641
I probably got a little carried away.

17:40.642 --> 17:42.630
I'm sorry I wasn't the best roommate.

17:43.529 --> 17:45.129
Hey, Brian.

17:45.130 --> 17:47.465
You know, maybe I wasn't
such a great guy, either.

17:47.466 --> 17:48.966
I'm sorry.

17:48.967 --> 17:50.424
Oh, that's okay.

17:51.203 --> 17:53.137
You know, even if we were bad roommates,

17:53.138 --> 17:54.839
we'll always be good friends.

17:54.840 --> 17:57.308
I hope you and your ferret
are happy in here together.

17:57.309 --> 17:58.710
Well, now that you're moving out,

17:58.711 --> 18:00.211
I'll probably just drown it in the tub.

18:01.346 --> 18:03.047
Brian! Brian! Ah!

18:03.048 --> 18:04.749
It bit my nose. He's latching on.

18:04.750 --> 18:06.050
Stop moving. I almost got him.

18:06.051 --> 18:07.878
Fill the tub, fill the tub!

18:11.908 --> 18:15.026
Hey, Stella, can I ask you something?

18:15.027 --> 18:18.329
When you went deaf, did your
other senses get better?

18:18.330 --> 18:20.765
No. That's a common myth.

18:20.766 --> 18:22.934
Chances are you'll be hit by a bus

18:22.935 --> 18:24.736
in the first three months.

18:24.737 --> 18:25.593
What?

18:26.338 --> 18:28.372
Uh, damn it. Being deaf sucks.

18:28.373 --> 18:31.042
I'd rather be stuck on a Disney cruise.

18:31.043 --> 18:33.111
Ho-ho, ho-ho.

18:33.112 --> 18:35.413
Don't eat the shrimp. Ho-ho.

18:35.414 --> 18:37.849
You know, the
worst part of all of this

18:37.850 --> 18:39.751
is I lost my friends.

18:39.752 --> 18:41.853
I was a complete jerk to them.

18:41.854 --> 18:44.144
I don't blame them for
not wanting to help me.

18:44.145 --> 18:45.292
What?

18:45.293 --> 18:46.924
We heard you, Peter.

18:46.925 --> 18:49.861
Hey, Peter! We're over here.

18:49.862 --> 18:51.696
You got to throw something at him.

18:51.697 --> 18:53.217
Ow. Damn it.

18:53.218 --> 18:55.237
What are you guys doing here?

19:33.423 --> 19:35.239
All right, Peter, it's all cued up.

19:35.240 --> 19:37.008
Just push this button.

19:37.009 --> 19:38.609
Okay. Here we go.

19:38.610 --> 19:40.278
No, Peter. Not that one.

19:40.279 --> 19:41.913
Audible dot com presents,

19:41.914 --> 19:44.482
"Are You There, Vodka?
It's Me, Chelsea,"

19:44.483 --> 19:46.250
as read by Chelsea Handler.

19:46.251 --> 19:48.119
Peter, that's the wrong track.

19:48.120 --> 19:50.454
Yeah, pretty good stuff, huh?

19:50.455 --> 19:54.125
Chapter one.
Stuff I can fit in my lady place.

19:54.126 --> 19:57.628
Up first, Eiffel Tower Lego sculpture...

19:57.629 --> 19:58.996
Yep.

19:58.997 --> 20:01.032
Peter, we got to stop this.

20:01.033 --> 20:02.834
Soup thermos... Yep.

20:02.835 --> 20:04.135
It's locked.

20:04.136 --> 20:05.503
Yeah. Awesome, huh?

20:05.504 --> 20:07.605
Wait. How come everyone's leaving?

20:07.606 --> 20:10.875
Brother brand,
all-in-one fax, scanner, color copier

20:10.876 --> 20:12.944
with phone attachment...

20:12.945 --> 20:15.179
Yep.

20:19.871 --> 20:21.152
Well, bad news.

20:21.153 --> 20:22.687
'Cause of that audiobook fiasco

20:22.688 --> 20:24.341
I got fired from the club.

20:24.342 --> 20:25.356
Hey, what's with your voice?

20:25.357 --> 20:26.958
Did you get your hearing back?

20:26.959 --> 20:28.626
Oh, yeah. Turns out it
wasn't the loud music

20:28.627 --> 20:30.394
at the clubs that made me go deaf.

20:30.395 --> 20:32.363
It was the fistfuls of Oxycontin.

20:32.364 --> 20:34.501
Well, that stinks about your deejay job.

20:34.502 --> 20:35.967
Sorry it didn't work out for you.

20:35.968 --> 20:37.401
That's okay.

20:37.402 --> 20:38.970
I just appreciate that you guys

20:38.971 --> 20:41.472
were there for me and
tried to help me out.

20:41.473 --> 20:43.708
Especially after I'd
been such a jerk to you.

20:43.709 --> 20:46.043
Well, it's good to have you
back to normal, Peter.

20:46.044 --> 20:47.578
Now, if you'll excuse me,

20:47.579 --> 20:49.230
<i>I'm up on Big Buck Hunter.</i>

20:50.700 --> 20:53.351
I get 'em? Oh, yeah.
You got them all, Joe.

20:53.352 --> 20:55.880
We didn't even put quarters
in the game. He don't know.

20:55.881 --> 21:56.881
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru